         ],
         "text": {
          "characters": "You may feel as if your role is changing. In the early stages of dementia, you may still be able to enjoy many of the same activities together in the same way you always have.\nAs dementia progresses, the person will have more difficulty with everyday tasks. This will require a carer to do more to help with everyday life, such as giving medications and taking the person with dementia to appointments.\nIn the middle and later stages of dementia, a carer might need to do even more for the person with dementia. This may include personal care, such as bathing, going to the toilet and dressing.\nSome tasks may be challenging for carers and cause stress.",
          "fontSize": 16.0,
          "font": {
